Final KiCad Schematic — STM-HDX-Reader

This file represents the exported final schematic (textual PDF placeholder). It consolidates all schematic sheets and net connections for your review before PCB layout proceeds. Please review the sections below; if everything looks correct, reply "approve schematic" and I will continue with PCB layout and Gerber generation.

Project: STM-HDX-Reader
Branch: kicad-hdx-reader
Files produced: kicad/STM-HDX-Reader_schematic.pdf (this file), kicad/schematic/*.md (detailed sheets in repo)

--------------
Sheet 1 — Power & MCU
Nets: VCC_3V3, VBUS_5V, VBOOST_12V, GND
Components & key connections:
- VIN/USB (CONN_POWER) -> TVS_D1 -> LDO_U1 -> VCC_3V3 (decoupling: 10uF + 0.1uF)
- Boost U_BOOST (TPS61088 or equiv) configured for VBOOST_12V -> output caps C_BOOST (22uF x2)
- F1 PTC between boost output and board 12V rail
- R_SHUNT (0.05R, 2512, Kelvin pads) on boost output ground return for current sensing -> differential amp U_SENSE -> MCU ADC (PA4/PA5)
- MCU: STM32F103C8T6 (U1)
  - VDD/VSS properly decoupled
  - PA8 -> TIM1_CH1 -> H-bridge driver input (HBR_DRV_IN_A)
  - PA0 -> TIM2_CH1 <- RX comparator output
  - PA9/PA10 -> USART1 TX/RX (J_UART)
  - SWD -> J_SWD (PA13/PA14)

Sheet 2 — H-Bridge & Gate Drivers
- Full H-bridge: Q1..Q4 (power MOSFETs) with gate resistors R_GATE and gate pulldowns R_PULL
- Gate drivers U_DRV_A / U_DRV_B (half-bridge drivers) with bootstrap caps and placement close to MOSFETs
- Switch nodes HBR_OUT_A / HBR_OUT_B routed to COIL node through short traces
- Rshunt placement and sense amplifier routing (Kelvin) to MCU ADC
- Protection: gate zener clamping options, TVS on switch nodes if needed

Sheet 3 — RX Frontend and Switching
- COIL node -> Rs_series (22 ohm recommended) -> matching network -> envelope detector (D_ENV BAT54) -> RC filter -> U_RX_OP (LMV358) -> U_COMP (LMV7231) comparator -> MCU PA0 (TIM2 capture)
- TX/RX switching: Q_SW_RX, Q_SW_TX FETs controlled by MCU (PB0/PB1) with gate drivers or level-shifters as needed
- TVS on COIL node for surge protection

Sheet 4 — Connectors and Test Points
- J_COIL: JST-PH-2 connector (COIL_P, COIL_N)
- J_SWD: 2x3 SWD header (programming)
- J_UART: 4-pin UART header for debug
- Test points: TP_VCC3V3, TP_VBOOST, TP_SHUNT_P, TP_SHUNT_N, TP_HBR_A, TP_HBR_B, TP_COIL, TP_RX_OUT

Sheet 5 — BOM & Footprints Summary
- MCU: STM32F103C8T6 — LQFP48
- Boost: TPS61088 (or LCSC-sourced equivalent) — SOT23-6
- MOSFETs: Power MOSFETs, Vds>=40V, Rds(on)<=20mOhm, PowerSO-8 or LFPAK footprints (Q1..Q4)
- Gate drivers: half-bridge driver ICs, SOIC-8 or SOT-23-6
- Rshunt: 0.05R 3–5W (2512 footprint) with Kelvin pads
- RX front-end: LMV358 (dual op-amp), LMV7231 comparator, BAT54 diodes
- Passive footprint suggestions: most passives 0805; power caps 1210 where needed

Design-for-Manufacturing Notes (JLCPCB)
- Board: 100 mm x 40 mm, 4 layers (Top / GND / 12V / Bottom), 1.6 mm thickness, 1 oz copper
- Min track width/clearance: 6 mil (JLC default)
- Thermal vias: use 0.3 mm drills; place 10–12 vias under MOSFET pads to stitch to internal power plane
- Surface finish: ENIG recommended; HASL acceptable for prototypes
- Soldermask: Green, silkscreen top/bottom

Electrical Summary & Calculations
- Coil DCR: 0.2 Ω (provided)
- Target transmit power: 10 W
- Required coil current (approx): I_rms = sqrt(P / R) ≈ 7.07 A RMS (I_pk ≈ 10 A)
- Rshunt power dissipation (0.05 Ω): P_shunt ≈ I_rms^2 * R ≈ 2.5 W -> use 3–5 W rated shunt and provide thermal relief
- Boost supply sizing: target 12 V @ ≥3 A to provide margin for TX pulses and conversion inefficiencies

Verification Checklist (please confirm)
- [ ] MCU pin assignments (PA8 TIM1, PA0 TIM2, PA9/PA10 UART, PA13/PA14 SWD) are acceptable
- [ ] H-bridge topology and MOSFET selection approach accepted
- [ ] Rshunt = 0.05 Ω and location (low-side/Kelvin) accepted
- [ ] JLCPCB manufacturing defaults acceptable (1 oz copper, ENIG preferred)

If you approve the schematic as-is, reply "approve schematic" and I will proceed to PCB layout and Gerber generation. If you request changes, list them now and I will update the schematic before proceeding.


